# OWASP — backend

When editing backend code, enforce from `code-review/data/owasp-checklist.json`:

- Parameterized PostgreSQL queries only (`$1`, ORM bind params)
- Server-side validation on every endpoint (Zod/class-validator at boundary)
- Auth middleware on protected routes; RBAC in services
- No secrets in code — use env / a managed secrets store
- Structured errors without internal details; audit log security events
- Rate-limit auth and sensitive endpoints

## Sensitive-data features — also apply `apply-security-patterns`

When the endpoint stores, reads, looks up, or exports sensitive/PII/financial data, read skill
`apply-security-patterns` and its checklist sections in `code-review/data/owasp-checklist.json`,
and apply:

- **Envelope encryption at rest** for sensitive columns (KEK in KMS/HSM → per-column DEK →
  AES-256-GCM with AAD bound to model+row+column); never a single flat app-held key
- **Keyed HMAC blind index** (own key, salted via a KDF) for encrypted values that must be looked up or deduped
- **Field-level projection** — select only needed columns; relationship/org-chart queries select no PII
- **Mask in lists, full value only on detail**; return aggregates (counts), not per-record sensitive values
- **Gate bulk export above browse** (elevated grant) + **audit-log** it (actor, filters, count)
- **Close enumeration oracles** — validate lookup input to full format before querying
- **Per-authenticated-actor rate limiters** (mounted after auth) on export, lookup, and list/search;
  independent counters per surface

Cross-check: `scan-dependency` before new packages.
